            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "creation_time": "2026-11-18T04:06:23Z",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 0,
            "text": "## Summary\n\nFunctions that decode a UTF-8 string one character at a time, such as `toupper()`, `encodeString()`, `format()` and `nchar(type = \"width\")`, take time quadratic in its number of non-ASCII characters: 2.6 s for `format()` of a 200,000-character string. Enhancement: a performance fix, results do not change.\n\n## Details\n\nBefore each multibyte form, `utf8toucs()` in `src/main/util.c` checks the remaining length with `strlen(s) < n`, which scans to the end of the string, and its callers call it once per character. Tested on R-devel r90925.\n\nReproducible example: attached as `utf8toucs-strlen-repro.R`; times the three functions as the string doubles: 4x as long per doubling before the patch, a few ms after.\n\nProposed patch: attached as `utf8toucs-strlen.diff`; a helper that looks only at the bytes the form needs, which gives the same answer as `strlen(s) < n`, plus a timing in `tests/reg-tests-1e.R`.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/510, where CI results can be seen.",
            "bug_id": 19338
          },
          {
