            "creation_time": "2026-11-18T04:32:27Z",
            "text": "Created attachment 4108\nPatch against r90925 (v2): drop the length checks in utf8toucs(); strsplit(perl = TRUE) passes the remaining length\n\nRevised patch attached, replacing attachment 4104. Rather than swap the `strlen(s) < n` checks in `utf8toucs()` for a helper, it removes them: they were never needed to stay in bounds, since NUL is never a continuation byte and each branch tests its continuation bytes in order with `&&`. They only made a truncated sequence return `(size_t)-2` instead of `-1`. The one caller that tells the two apart, `mbcsToSbcs()` in `devPS.c`, mishandles `-2` (under ASan, `pdf()` text ending in `\"\\xf0\"` gives negative-size-param) and now takes its invalid-input path.\n\nThe patch also fixes the same pattern in `strsplit(perl = TRUE)`, which ran `strlen()` on the rest of the string for every piece: 1.3 s for 200,000 pieces, 0.013 s after.\n\nPatch also at https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/510",
            "bug_id": 19338,
            "count": 3,
